\title{Odd squares, again}
\date{2026-02-11T14:20:53Z}
\tag{discrete}
\tag{draft}
\taxon{Example}

\import{discrete-macros}

\p{Prove: #{\all{n}{\Z} \Odd(n) \iff \Odd(n^2).}}

\proof{
  Let #{k} be an arbitrary integer; we will prove #{\Odd(k) \iff \Odd(k^2)}.  To prove this biconditional, we will prove both directions.

  \subproof{
    #{\Odd(k) \to \Odd(k^2)}.  We [already proved this above](005L).
  }

  \subproof{
    #{\Odd(k^2) \to \Odd(k)}.

    Try; fail; use contrapositive (+ assumption for now that #{\neg \Odd \equiv \Even})
  }
}
